Company punishment.

26
00:02:44,520 --> 00:02:46,351
More stubble.

27
00:02:46,520 --> 00:02:49,318
- When did you shave, soldier?
- I shaved last night, sir.

28
00:02:49,480 --> 00:02:53,632
Army regulations say
you will shave every morning.

29
00:02:53,800 --> 00:02:56,030
Company punishment.

30
00:03:01,360 --> 00:03:04,158
Tell me you're feeling
better today, private.

31
00:03:04,320 --> 00:03:05,992
Yes, sir.

32
00:03:46,200 --> 00:03:48,156
Sergeant.

33
00:03:51,200 --> 00:03:52,679
Sir.

34
00:04:10,480 --> 00:04:12,550
Well, troopers,

35
00:04:12,720 --> 00:04:15,075
looks like you messed up again,

36
00:04:15,240 --> 00:04:17,754
which means field exercises again.

37
00:04:18,080 --> 00:04:20,992
Tonight, 1 800 hours.

38
00:04:21,160 --> 00:04:22,798
Sound good to you?

39
00:04:22,960 --> 00:04:25,030
Yes, sir.

40
00:04:25,480 --> 00:04:29,155
- You can thank whoever left this.
- Sir.

41
00:04:29,320 --> 00:04:30,992
Thomas and I
just cleaned the latrine, sir.

42
00:04:31,160 --> 00:04:32,593
There was no cigarette butt in there.

43
00:04:32,760 --> 00:04:35,832
Then maybe you're the ones
that they should thank.

44
00:04:45,840 --> 00:04:46,875
At ease.

45
00:04:47,040 --> 00:04:49,395
That lousy...

46
00:04:49,560 --> 00:04:51,869
Bobby, Bobby, you okay?

47
00:04:52,040 --> 00:04:53,917
Stomach cramps again, man.

48
00:04:54,080 --> 00:04:56,150
If it was something you ate,
you'd be over it by now.

49
00:04:56,320 --> 00:04:57,799
It's gotta be some kind of a bug.

50
00:04:58,400 --> 00:05:00,038
Maybe so.

51
00:05:00,200 --> 00:05:03,510
Maybe the next one to get it
will be Walters, you know?

52
00:05:05,880 --> 00:05:08,440
Forget it, Bobby. You're not
going out in the field tonight.

53
00:05:08,600 --> 00:05:10,079
You go on sick call.

54
00:05:10,240 --> 00:05:13,676
And face Walters?
No, man. No way.

55
00:05:13,840 --> 00:05:16,479
Crawling around in the dark
is a picnic compared to Walters.

56
00:05:18,800 --> 00:05:20,518
Yeah.

57
00:05:21,600 --> 00:05:24,398
Go! Out of there! Come on!
Hustle, hustle!

58
00:05:24,560 --> 00:05:27,233
I got a grandmother
who moves faster than you!

59
00:05:27,400 --> 00:05:29,391
Come on!

60
00:05:31,320 --> 00:05:32,992
All right, gentlemen,

61
00:05:33,600 --> 00:05:36,068
observe the wooded area
in front of you.

62
00:05:36,240 --> 00:05:38,959
C Company made it
across that terrain and back

63
00:05:39,120 --> 00:05:41,111
in two hours and 1 7 minutes.

64
00:05:41,720 --> 00:05:43,597
That used to be the fort record.

65
00:05:43,760 --> 00:05:48,072
I say ''used to be'' because you
are going to make it across and back

66
00:05:48,240 --> 00:05:50,549
in two hours and ten minutes.

67
00:05:50,880 --> 00:05:53,235
- Got it?
- Yes, sir!

68
00:05:53,400 --> 00:05:54,389
Then move them out.

69
00:05:54,560 --> 00:05:59,759
Left face, double-time march.

70
00:06:21,560 --> 00:06:23,152
Bobby? Bobby, come on.

71
00:06:23,320 --> 00:06:25,914
Move it, Thomas, move it.
What, your skirt get wet? Come on.

72
00:06:26,080 --> 00:06:29,231
- Lay off him. He's got cramps again.
- I'm okay.

73
00:06:29,400 --> 00:06:32,551
Bobby, you can't do this.
Go back. Forget about Walters.

74
00:06:33,920 --> 00:06:36,309
Hey, hey! Where do you think
you're going, Thomas?

75
00:06:36,480 --> 00:06:38,038
Where do you think you're going?
Thomas!

76
00:06:38,200 --> 00:06:40,316
He's sick, sarge.

77
00:07:12,400 --> 00:07:14,118
What are you doing here?

78
00:07:14,280 --> 00:07:16,999
- Sir, I can't continue the exercise.
- Get back out there.

79
00:07:17,160 --> 00:07:20,311
Sir, I'm sick. My insides are cramping
so bad I can hardly move.

80
00:07:20,480 --> 00:07:24,075
I'm the one who's getting sick
of mama's boys like you.

81
00:07:24,240 --> 00:07:26,800
Your soul may belong to God,
Thomas, but your butt belongs to me,

82
00:07:26,960 --> 00:07:29,838
and if you don't move it on out there
on the double and rejoin that unit,

83
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:32,878
I am gonna teach you what pain is.
Is that what you want?

84
00:07:33,040 --> 00:07:34,837
- No, sir.
- Then move out!

85
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:36,194
I'll never catch up now.

86
00:07:36,360 --> 00:07:39,796
Follow that stream, about 200 yards,
cross it, head west,

87
00:07:39,960 --> 00:07:42,713
and you'll cut them off.
Now, haul it!

88
00:07:53,040 --> 00:07:55,031
Fall out.

89
00:08:04,800 --> 00:08:05,994
All right, listen up.

90
00:08:06,400 --> 00:08:08,436
Two hours

91
00:08:08,600 --> 00:08:12,195
and 21 minutes.

92
00:08:13,200 --> 00:08:16,237
Guess we'll just have to do this
more often.

93
00:08:16,400 --> 00:08:19,790
You do wanna break that record,
don't you?

94
00:08:19,960 --> 00:08:22,679
- Yes, sir.
- All right.

95
00:08:22,840 --> 00:08:24,068
Smoke them if you got them.

96
00:08:26,400 --> 00:08:27,958
Where's Thomas, sir?

97
00:08:29,240 --> 00:08:31,515
I sent the pansy back out.

98
00:08:31,680 --> 00:08:34,274
Back out where?
He's not with us, sir.

99
00:08:36,920 --> 00:08:40,435
All right, everybody.
Back on your feet.

100
00:08:40,600 --> 00:08:43,876
Fan out over the line of march
and locate Private Thomas.

101
00:08:44,040 --> 00:08:47,237
Everybody up! Come on! Let's go!

102
00:08:47,400 --> 00:08:49,072
Move!

103
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:53,070
You had no business sending him
back out there.

104
00:08:53,240 --> 00:08:54,673
He was sick.

105
00:08:54,880 --> 00:08:56,996
You arguing with me soldier?

106
00:08:57,160 --> 00:08:59,435
- I'm just telling you, sir.
- Shut up.

107
00:09:00,120 --> 00:09:02,475
And go find your little friend.

108
00:09:12,240 --> 00:09:14,037
Thomas!

109
00:09:15,520 --> 00:09:18,034
Bobby! Bobby!

110
00:09:18,680 --> 00:09:20,398
Bobby!

111
00:09:22,200 --> 00:09:24,111
Bobby!

112
00:09:24,280 --> 00:09:26,271
- Thomas!
- Bobby!

113
00:09:26,440 --> 00:09:28,078
Bobby!

114
00:09:28,680 --> 00:09:30,238
Bobby!

115
00:09:30,680 --> 00:09:31,829
Bobby!

116
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:34,639
Hey, he's over here! Get a medic!

117
00:09:34,800 --> 00:09:36,438
Bobby.

118
00:10:01,320 --> 00:10:02,912
Can I help you?

119
00:10:09,560 --> 00:10:11,437
Hey, kid, this place
would be off-limits to you

120
00:10:11,600 --> 00:10:13,158
even if we didn't have a dress code.

121
00:10:13,320 --> 00:10:14,355
I'm talking to you.

122
00:10:15,360 --> 00:10:16,429
You lost, soldier?

123
00:10:16,600 --> 00:10:18,955
Bobby Thomas' appendix
ruptured tonight.

124
00:10:19,120 --> 00:10:22,271
I just came from the hospital.
Bobby's dead and you killed him.

125
00:10:22,440 --> 00:10:23,509
At ease, Hughes.

126
00:10:23,680 --> 00:10:25,477
- You go to hell!
- That's enough, private.

127
00:10:25,840 --> 00:10:28,673
- You're addressing an officer.
- He's not fit to be an officer.

128
00:10:28,840 --> 00:10:30,273
He killed one of his own men.

129
00:10:30,440 --> 00:10:32,829
Bobby Thomas died tonight
because you sent him back out there

130
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:35,912
- even though you knew he was sick.
- Get out.

131
00:10:37,840 --> 00:10:39,671
You're easier to read
than Mother Goose.

132
00:10:44,960 --> 00:10:46,154
Lieutenant.

133
00:10:46,480 --> 00:10:47,674
Sit down.

134
00:10:51,760 --> 00:10:55,150
- You're gonna pay.
- At ease, private. That's an order.

135
00:10:55,320 --> 00:10:56,355
They're gonna investigate.

136
00:10:56,520 --> 00:10:59,114
I'm gonna tell them what happened.
They're finally gonna nail you.

137
00:10:59,280 --> 00:11:02,352
Private Hughes, you will consider
yourself confined to quarters.

138
00:11:02,520 --> 00:11:04,954
- Do I make myself clear?
- Yes, sir.

139
00:11:10,840 --> 00:11:12,671
My God, Ray.

140
00:11:15,880 --> 00:11:17,677
As he said,

141
00:11:18,960 --> 00:11:21,394
there will be an investigation.

142
00:11:22,280 --> 00:11:24,316
Walters.

143
00:11:24,520 --> 00:11:27,671
Ever consider that maybe
you push your luck?

144
